  "description": "Like for like replacement of single glazed timber sash and casement windows with identical double glazed timber Heritage \"Slimline\" glazing units. \nAs per specification attached, glazing is 4mm with 6mm Argon filled gap, total width 14mm. White spacer bars match white colour of frames.\nDesign, materials, detailing, integral glazing bars and opening mechanism replicate the current windows. No trickle vents.\nSt James School is located in a Conservation area. Flat 6 is located on east side of St James School on 2nd and 3rd floors as shown by blue marker on location plan.\nWorks would be carried out by the attached reputable supplier, FENSA member and Which? Trusted Trader.\nReplacements in accordance with recommendations in London Borough of Islington's \"Guide to Repairing and Upgrading Windows in Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas\" , section 3.6, \"Replacing Traditional Windows with Double Glazed Units\".\n",
